          <type>const <ref refid="classecss_1_1ArraysView" kindref="compound">ArraysView</ref> &amp;</type>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>A view is a fixed place, not a value. Its cached begin iterator points into the view&apos;s own mRanges, so a copy or a move would leave that iterator addressing the original <ndash/> dangling the moment the original dies. The structural holds it carries have the same shape of problem as AccessGuard&apos;s: they are released against per-thread bookkeeping, so a second owner would release what it never took.</para>
<para>Nothing is lost by this. <ref refid="classecss_1_1Registry_1a9e5e54a8233e370ccfa8585538bf7ab7" kindref="member">Registry::view()</ref> returns a prvalue, so <computeroutput>auto v = reg.view&lt;T&gt;()</computeroutput> and iterating a temporary both go through guaranteed elision and never needed either. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="ecss/Registry.h" line="1990" column="1"/>
