        <detaileddescription>
<para>This is a join, and that is the difference from iterating the view with a range-for. Here func takes references and is called, in view iteration order, only for entities that have every named component; one missing secondary skips the entity. A range-for yields (EntityId, T*, CompTypes*...) for every entity with the main component, and a secondary it lacks arrives as nullptr for you to test.</para>
<para>Pick <ref refid="classecss_1_1ArraysView_1a1b74ea714c01e4178e4063aaa504d50b" kindref="member">each()</ref> when the entity is only interesting with all of them, and the range-for when a missing component means something to your code. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
